; The high band's noise. Per frame in: V and the frame's level (the record of the high-band table that choose's
; filter names), then the next frame's V and level (the host deals the records again from the second frame on). Out,
; for each of the frame's ten steps, 120 samples at 48 kHz of +L or -L, by the sign of x - 500, where x runs through
; the decimal LCG x = 21 x + 7 mod 1000 (21 x as 10 x + 10 x + x, mod 1000 by STO), as excite's does. At the start of
; each step x is moved on by w, which runs through the same LCG a step at a time, so that the noise doesn't repeat
; every 1,000 samples. L starts at the frame's level and moves on by (next - this) / 10 a step (SFT 01), as interp
; and steps move A, and not at all when the next frame's V differs. A step whose L is 0 puts out 120 0s.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            frm     INP   v        03-20: a frame, and its step: (next - this) / 10, or 0
  04                    INP   h
  05                    INP   nv
  06                    INP   nh
  07                    CLA   z
  08                    STO   d
  09                    CLA   nv
  10                    SUB   v
  11                    TAC   go
  12                    SUB   00
  13                    TAC   same
  14                    JMP   go
  15            same    CLA   nh
  16                    SUB   h
  17                    SFT   01
  18                    STO   d
  19            go      CLA   n9
  20                    STO   k
  21            step    CLA   x        21-36: a step: x = x + w, w = 21 w + 7, and L 0 or not
  22                    ADD   w
  23                    STO   x
  24                    CLA   w
  25                    SFT   10
  26                    STO   t
  27                    CLA   t
  28                    ADD   t
  29                    ADD   w
  30                    ADD   seven
  31                    STO   w
  32                    CLA   n119
  33                    STO   c
  34                    CLA   h
  35                    SUB   00
  36                    TAC   quiet
  37            smp     CLA   x        37-58: a sample, +L or -L
  38                    SFT   10
  39                    STO   t
  40                    CLA   t
  41                    ADD   t
  42                    ADD   x
  43                    ADD   seven
  44                    STO   x
  45                    CLA   x
  46                    SUB   c500
  47                    TAC   neg
  48                    OUT   h
  49                    JMP   nxs
  50            neg     CLA   z
  51                    SUB   h
  52                    STO   t
  53                    OUT   t
  54            nxs     CLA   c
  55                    SUB   00
  56                    STO   c
  57                    TAC   endst
  58                    JMP   smp
  59            quiet   OUT   z        59-64: a step of 0s
  60                    CLA   c
  61                    SUB   00
  62                    STO   c
  63                    TAC   endst
  64                    JMP   quiet
  65            endst   CLA   h        65-87: L moves on; ten steps a frame
  66                    ADD   d
  67                    STO   h
  68                    CLA   k
  69                    SUB   00
  70                    STO   k
  71                    TAC   frm
  72                    JMP   step
  73            v       DATA  0
  74            h       DATA  0
  75            nv      DATA  0
  76            nh      DATA  0
  77            d       DATA  0
  78            k       DATA  0
  79            c       DATA  0
  80            x       DATA  123
  81            w       DATA  0
  82            t       DATA  0
  83            z       DATA  0
  84            seven   DATA  7
  85            c500    DATA  500
  86            n9      DATA  9
  87            n119    DATA  119
